<title>UK: UK,Bombardier unit reach compensation deal.</title>
<headline>UK,Bombardier unit reach compensation deal.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The government has reached an agreement with Airwork Services, a unit of Bombardier Inc's Short Brothers subsidiary, on compensation caused to air force Tornado aircraft it was servicing, government sources said.</p>
<p>They said details of the accord will be announced in a written parliamentary answer from the Defence Ministry at or shortly after 1530 gmt.</p>
<p>In 1993, the ministry cancelled a contract with Airwork for the servicing of Tornados. British newspapers have reported that 16 of the aircraft were damaged, and that the government had to spend some 100 million stg putting the matter right.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 5427767</p>
